{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And you shall give it.</b> It says <b>otah</b> — according to what our Rabbis of blessed memory said (Parah 4:1), that from the oral tradition they learned that other cows [red heifers] may be prepared whether by the High Priest or by an ordinary priest, [therefore] it was necessary to say ״אוֹתָהּ אֶל אֶלְעָזָר״ — but from this point onward there is no obligation [for it to be done by] the deputy [High Priest]."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {0 "The word סְגָן here refers to the deputy High Priest; the point is that beyond the initial giving to Elazar, the remaining procedures do not require specifically the segan."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:10:57.360914588Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}